Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["PN data: binding energy", "Chapter",ExpressionUUID->"40429aba-a545-44b6-a9b8-415d7fd3265d"],

Cell["\<\
Source: PNpedia (commit a64de8b), Circular \
orbits/Spinning/Nonprecessing/Without tidal effects/Constants of \
motion/Energy/energy_conservative.txt, black holes (\[Kappa] = \[Lambda] = \
1). Nonspinning and SO/SS 4PN from arXiv:1401.4548, 1711.00283, 2201.05138; \
SSS 3.5PN from arXiv:1411.4118; quartic-in-spin terms vanish at 4PN.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b3114c70-561b-4aa2-97e8-fc181c1898da"],

Cell["\<\
Conservative (mechanical) energy, not PNpedia's energy_binding.txt: Honet \
replaces the Bondi mass with the mechanical energy and leaves out the 4PN \
Schott term (Sec. III C). The binding version adds the b0-dependent Schott \
term, which only cancels against a matching flux; the Blanchet+2023 4PN flux \
of HybridEnFluxes.nb has no b0 and pairs with the conservative energy. The \
Checks chapter verifies binding = conservative + Schott.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"60dae917-adec-48df-911b-e59563dcaa79"],

Cell["\<\
Coefficients are relative to the Newtonian -\[Nu] M x/2. Spin variables as in \
PNpedia: s = S/M^2 = (m1^2 \[Chi]1 + m2^2 \[Chi]2)/M^2, sg = \
\[CapitalSigma]/M^2 = (m2 \[Chi]2 - m1 \[Chi]1)/M, dl = \[CapitalDelta] = (m1 \
- m2)/M.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a0da7da2-2d5f-4d01-a3df-ca0da9505012"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Nonspinning 4PN", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"8a7333c0-85f9-400e-85fc-edb432d04260"],

Cell["The 4.5PN terms vanish for circular orbits. lx = Log[x].", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"174dde72-de17-49e4-ae3c-670b5b42f692"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
